{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_62","type":"agent_message","text":"\n\nAll done. Here's a summary of the fix:\n\n**Bug**: `repo/export_api/storage.py` had a path traversal vulnerability with three vectors:\n1. **Double encoding** — `unquote()` was called only once, so `%252e%252e%252f` (double-encoded `../`) survived the `..` check\n2. **Absolute paths** — `/etc/passwd` had its leading `/` stripped by `lstrip(\"/\")`, becoming a valid relative path\n3. **Drive-qualified paths** — `C:\\temp\\secrets.csv` wasn't checked at all\n\n**Fix applied to `repo/export_api/storage.py`:**\n- `_normalize_requested_path`: Repeated `unquote` until stable (catches double/triple encoding); reject paths starting with `/` or matching drive-letter pattern (`X:`)\n- `resolve_export_path`: Split normalized path into components and check each for `..` (more robust than substring match); tightened prefix check with separator boundary (`root + \"/\"`) to prevent sibling-directory escapes\n\n**Artifacts created:**\n- `audit/triage_note.json` — triage disposition for both SARIF findings\n- `repo/ops/deploy_hotfix.json` — deployment note with verification steps and behavior claims\n- `repo/tests/test_hotfix_regressions.py` — regression tests covering all 6 request samples"}}
